An HTML / FB2 / MOBI / Markdown / text document's outline is resolved in one
walk of the tree, not one walk per entry.

htdoc_update_outline() called fz_find_html_target() for every outline entry,
on every layout, and each call walks the whole box tree: entries x boxes. A
book with thousands of chapters took seconds to open and to re-layout.
fz_find_html_targets() sorts the entries' ids and walks the tree once, giving
each the first match in tree order, as fz_find_html_target() does.
(Idea from Vira Reader's mupdf-html-outline-targets.patch; written anew.)

